cards.back:
```python
class Report:
    def __init__(self, title, content):
        self.title = title
        self.content = content

    def get_title(self):
        return self.title

    def get_content(self):
        return self.content

class ReportFormatter:
    def format_html(self, report: Report):
        return f"<h1>{report.get_title()}</h1><p>{report.get_content()}</p>"

    def format_plain_text(self, report: Report):
        return f"--- {report.get_title()} ---\n{report.get_content()}"

class ReportRepository:
    def save(self, report: Report):
        print(f"Saving report '{report.get_title()}' to DB...")
        # DB saving logic here
```
Now, `Report` only holds data, `ReportFormatter` handles formatting, and `ReportRepository` handles persistence. Each has one reason to change.
